  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Multi-sectoral humanitarian assistance to address the most urgent needs of conflict-affected people in Northwest</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ltpgtltspangtThe Northwest (NW) region of Myanmar, has seen a sharp increase in conflict and displacement, resulting in critical and timely humanitarian responses to be set-up in the region. The overall objective of the project is to address the most urgent and unmet humanitarian needs of&#xA0;&#xA0;24,208 total (5,308 men, 6,427 women, 5811 boys and 6662 girls)&#xA0; conflict-affected IDPs and host communities in hard-to-reach and underserved areas in Chin (Falam, Hakha, Mindat and Thantlang), Sagaing (Ayadaw, Kalay, Maw Laik, Myin Mu, Phaung Byin and Pin Le Bu), and Magway (Gangaw, Saw and Seik Phyu). With a focus on people with specific vulnerabilities, including those linked to age, gender, disabilities or other characteristics of marginalization.&#xA0;&#xA0;lt/spangtltbrgtlt/pgt

ltpgtThis will be done through the provision of multisectoral
assistance in Education in Emergencies (EiE), Water, Sanitation, and Hygiene
(WASH), Shelter/Non-Food Items (NFI), Protection, and Food Security. The
intervention further builds on the MHF funded projects of PIN in Northwest (MM-21/DDA-3415/SA2/E-P-SNFI-WASH/INGO/20764
and MM-22/DDA-3415/RA2/E-SNFI-WASH-P/INGO/23092), and will utilize the already
existing human resources and humanitarian access pathways to deliver immediate
assistance to the vulnerable communities lt/pgt

ltpgtThe implementation strategy has been structured around
schools and the surrounding communities, integrating sectors to provide
holistic response packages to meet the most urgent unmet humanitarian needs
across the NW. Building on the strengths of the previous MHF project and the
resulting community feedback, this approach enables PIN and its partners to
play to their greatest strengths while adapting the overall approach to better
encompass the requests of the communities in need and the objectives of the
allocation strategy. lt/pgt

ltpgtTo provide holistic, humanitarian programming, and to manage
the critical access and security concerns in the NW, a consortium has been
formed between People In Need (PIN), Mines Advisory Group (MAG), Karuna Mission
Social Solidarity - Hakha (KMSS-Hakha), Chin Human Rights Organization (CHRO),
Servant of Agape Love (SOAL), and (SVP) who are currently operational and
present in NW.lt/pgt





ltpgtlt/pgt</narrative>
